{"name":"Ghosting","hex":"#cac6ba","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ghosting","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A method of ending a personal relationship by stopping any contact with the other party and not providing an explanation. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The blurry appearance of a television picture resulting from interference caused by multipath reception."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of ghost"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ghosting"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ghosting (identity theft)","blocks":[{"text":"Ghosting is a form of identity theft in which someone steals the identity, and sometimes even the role within society, of a specific dead person whose death is not widely known. Usually, the person who steals this identity is roughly the same age that the ghost would have been if still alive, so that any documents citing the birthdate of the ghost will not be conspicuously incorrect if appropriated by the thief now claiming to be that person."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghosting_(identity_theft)","wikidata":"Q17081207"},{"title":"Ghosting (behavior)","blocks":[{"text":"Ghosting is a colloquial term for the practice of suddenly ending all communication and avoiding contact with another person without any apparent warning or explanation and ignoring any subsequent attempts to communicate.\nWith increased digital communication, ghosting is often seen as an easy escape from confrontation or emotional discomfort, facilitated by the anonymity and convenience of online platforms."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghosting_(behavior)","wikidata":"Q21050182"},{"title":"Ghosting (television)","blocks":[{"text":"In television, a ghost is a replica of the transmitted image, offset in position, that is superimposed on top of the main image. It is often caused when a TV signal travels by two different paths to a receiving antenna, with a slight difference in timing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/TV_ghosting_interference.jpg/330px-TV_ghosting_interference.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghosting_(television)","wikidata":"Q551540"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Whatsapp_chatting_outdoor_20180808.jpg/500px-Whatsapp_chatting_outdoor_20180808.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Whatsapp_chatting_outdoor_20180808.jpg/1280px-Whatsapp_chatting_outdoor_20180808.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Whatsapp_chatting_outdoor_20180808.jpg/500px-Whatsapp_chatting_outdoor_20180808.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A person recreationally text messaging using WhatsApp","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhatsapp_chatting_outdoor_20180808.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/TV_ghosting_interference.jpg/500px-TV_ghosting_interference.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/TV_ghosting_interference.jpg/500px-TV_ghosting_interference.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A simulated example of severe ghosting in an analog TV broadcast","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATV_ghosting_interference.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/IdealTVpathnoghost.png/500px-IdealTVpathnoghost.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/IdealTVpathnoghost.png/500px-IdealTVpathnoghost.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ideal situation for TV signal propagation: The signal leaves the transmitter (TX) and travels through one path to the receiver (the TV set, which is labeled RX).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIdealTVpathnoghost.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/MultipathTVghost.png/500px-MultipathTVghost.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/MultipathTVghost.png/500px-MultipathTVghost.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An object (an aircraft) complicates the system by adding a second path. The signal arrives at RX by two paths which have different lengths. The main path is the direct path, while the second is a reflection from the plane.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMultipathTVghost.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/TV_ghost_eliminator.agr.jpg/500px-TV_ghost_eliminator.agr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/TV_ghost_eliminator.agr.jpg/1280px-TV_ghost_eliminator.agr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/TV_ghost_eliminator.agr.jpg/500px-TV_ghost_eliminator.agr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A \"ghost eliminator\" sold to consumers in the 1960s and 70s to make ghosting less visible. This unit was a simple resistive attenuator.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATV_ghost_eliminator.agr.jpg"}],"sounds":{"ghosting":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4c/En-au-ghosting.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/4c/En-au-ghosting.ogg/En-au-ghosting.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.5425},{"title":"José Clemente Orozco, La verdad 50, Pareja y fantasma","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Jos%C3%A9_Clemente_Orozco%2C_La_verdad_50%2C_Pareja_y_fantasma.jpg/500px-Jos%C3%A9_Clemente_Orozco%2C_La_verdad_50%2C_Pareja_y_fantasma.jpg","ratio":1.549090909090909,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jos%C3%A9_Clemente_Orozco,_La_verdad_50,_Pareja_y_fantasma.jpg","share":0.30375},{"title":"Werner's nomenclature of colours greys","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg/500px-Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","ratio":0.794047619047619,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","share":0.294375},{"title":"TheGhostAtPointOfRocks","image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/44/TheGhostAtPointOfRocks.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","ratio":0.6042003231017771,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TheGhostAtPointOfRocks.jpg","share":0.2675},{"title":"Grey Carpet from above","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Grey_Carpet_from_above.jpg/500px-Grey_Carpet_from_above.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_Carpet_from_above.jpg","share":0.16875},{"title":"HDR ghosting on bycicle","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/HDR_ghosting_on_bycicle.jpg/500px-HDR_ghosting_on_bycicle.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"h